IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain
IMPORT `g5-interpretation`
IMPORT `g5-nouns`

-- g5-art13-reporting.l4: Article 13(6) to (10) and (12) of the Charities (Jersey) Law 2014 -- what a registered charity must report to the
-- Commissioner, the annual return, and the Minister's and the States' powers over both.  Paragraphs (1) to (5), (11) and (13) are in
-- g5-art13-effects.  The quotations are copied mechanically from the Law's text file by srcrefs.py.
-- No Order or Regulations made under Article 13 is among the sources, so what any of them prescribes is an input: the matters prescribed
-- under (6)(h) and (7), the due date and the consequences of lateness (8), the payments and the statement (9), the relief (10).
-- Forks: F5.1 and F5.10 ("promptly"), F5.2, F5.11 and F5.13 (the year of the return and the date a matter arises), F5.3 (an "Order under
-- paragraph (8)"), F5.5 (a return sent on the due date); see g5-interpretation.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register`

§§ `13 Effects of registration`

§§§ `13(6) The matters a registered charity must promptly report`

-- A matter that falls within more than one paragraph is reported once; the rules below ask about one paragraph at a time, so a caller with such a matter
-- asks twice.  The Law states no number of days for "promptly" (period P8): the reading is the fork F5.1, and the number of days of readings 2 and 3 is
-- an input.  For (c) and (d) the matter may be a proposal, and "promptly" then runs from the proposal; the Law does not say whether a report made after
-- the change itself has been made still reports a proposal.

-- (a) to (h): does the matter fall within the paragraph?  The facts each paragraph turns on are the fields of the constructor; the standard inputs
-- 11(4)(c), 11(4)(d) and 12(1) are G4's, the reportable matters of a governor are G6's (field `reportable matters` of each `Governor`).
@ref Article 13(6)(e) (src:388)
GIVEN named IS A STRING
      governor IS A Governor
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6)(e) the governor is the one named and has a reportable matter` named governor MEANS
        governor's name EQUALS named
    AND NOT null (governor's `reportable matters`)

@ref Article 13(6)(e) (src:388)
GIVEN named IS A STRING
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6)(e) a governor of the charity is the one named and has a reportable matter` named `the registered charity` MEANS
    any (GIVEN governor YIELD `Art 13(6)(e) the governor is the one named and has a reportable matter` named governor)
        (`the registered charity`'s entity's governors)

-- src:384 | (a) a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register (whether in the general or restricted section) in relation to that charity;
-- src:385 | (b) any other matter, coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name, that could, if known before the registration or permission, have led to the Commissioner refusing to register the charity, refusing to accept the name of the charity, or entering it in a different section;
-- src:386 | (c) a proposal to change the charity’s constitution;
-- src:387 | (d) a proposal that could result, or an event that has resulted in the charity ceasing to meet the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d);
-- src:388 | (e) a reportable matter, in relation to a governor of the charity, if the charity is aware that the governor has not promptly reported it to the Commissioner under Article 19(2);
-- src:389 | (f) a matter likely to lead to the charity becoming bankrupt, being wound up or otherwise ceasing to exist;
-- src:390 | (g) if the charity is entered in the restricted section, a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets a condition prescribed under Article 9(2); and
-- src:391 | (h) any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(6)(a) to (h) (src:384-391)
@export Whether a matter falls within one of the paragraphs (a) to (h) of Article 13(6), so that a registered charity must promptly report it to the Commissioner
GIVEN `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including its governors and their reportable matters and the section it is entered in
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) (a Jersey entity, or a substantial activity in or from within Jersey)
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) (a principal address in Jersey)
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity's name is, on what is now known, undesirable under Article 12(1)
      matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)` @desc The matter and the facts its paragraph turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the registered charity` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` matter MEANS
    CONSIDER matter
    WHEN `a change in a matter about which information is entered on the register` entered changed
        THEN "(a)" ... entered AND changed
    WHEN `a matter coming to light after registration or after permission for a change of name` later cannotRegister differentSection
        THEN "(b)" ... later
             AND (   cannotRegister
                  OR `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)`
                  OR differentSection)
    WHEN `a proposal to change the charity's constitution` proposal
        THEN "(c)" ... proposal
    WHEN `a proposal or an event affecting the requirements of Article 11(4)(c) or (d)` proposal event
        THEN "(d)" ... (   proposal
                         OR (    event
                             AND (   NOT `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met`
                                  OR NOT `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met`)))
    WHEN `a reportable matter in relation to a governor` named aware
        THEN "(e)" ... aware
             AND `Art 13(6)(e) a governor of the charity is the one named and has a reportable matter` named `the registered charity`
    WHEN `a matter likely to lead to bankruptcy, winding up or ceasing to exist` likely
        THEN "(f)" ... likely
    WHEN `a proposal to change how or whether the charity meets its restricted-section condition` proposal
        THEN "(g)" ... `the registered charity`'s entity's `standing on the register` EQUALS `entered in the restricted section`
             AND proposal
    WHEN `a matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(6)(h)` within
        THEN "(h)" ... within

-- F5.10: when "promptly" is a number of days, is the day of the event counted?  Reading A (taken): not counted; reading B: it is the first day.
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE
      nDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F5.10 A: the last prompt day when the day of the event is not counted` anchor nDays MEANS
    anchor PLUS nDays

@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN anchor IS A DATE
      nDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F5.10 B: the last prompt day when the day of the event is the first day` anchor nDays MEANS
    anchor PLUS (nDays MINUS 1)

@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      anchor IS A DATE
      nDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 13(6) the last prompt day` interp anchor nDays MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether the day of the event counts in a number of days`
    WHEN `the day of the event is not counted: the last prompt day is the event day plus the number of days`
        THEN `F5.10 A: the last prompt day when the day of the event is not counted` anchor nDays
    WHEN `the day of the event is the first day: the last prompt day is one day earlier`
        THEN `F5.10 B: the last prompt day when the day of the event is the first day` anchor nDays

-- The last day on which a report is in time, if "promptly" is a number of days (NOTHING when it is an input judgement).
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`Art 13(6) the last day on which a report is in time` interp timing MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how promptness is measured`
    WHEN `an input judgement that the report was made promptly` THEN NOTHING
    WHEN `a number of days from the event or proposal` nDays
        THEN JUST (`Art 13(6) the last prompt day` interp (timing's `date of the event or proposal`) nDays)
    WHEN `a number of days from the charity becoming aware of the matter` nDays
        THEN JUST (`Art 13(6) the last prompt day` interp (timing's `date the charity became aware of the matter`) nDays)

-- src:383 | (6) A registered charity must promptly report to the Commissioner –
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
@export Whether a report of a matter under Article 13(6) was made promptly, on the reading of "promptly" given: an input judgement, or within a number of days of the event or proposal, or within a number of days of the charity becoming aware of the matter
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.1 decides what promptly means, and F5.10 how the days are counted
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` @desc The day of the event or proposal and the day the charity became aware of the matter
      report IS A `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` @desc The day the report was made, if it was, and the judgement that it was prompt
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(6) the report was made promptly` interp timing report MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 13(6) the last day on which a report is in time` interp timing
    WHEN NOTHING THEN report's `the report was made promptly`
    WHEN JUST lastDay THEN
        CONSIDER report's `date the report was made`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST reported THEN reported AT MOST lastDay

-- The duty, one implementation per reading of F5.1.  Reading A (taken): "promptly" is a standard, not a number of days, so the rule carries no WITHIN
-- and the promptness of the report is the input judgement; an act of reporting that is not prompt is not performance.
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)`
      report IS A `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`F5.1 A: report the matter, promptness being an input judgement` matter report MEANS
    PARTY `a registered charity`
    MUST `report a matter to the Commissioner` matter
         PROVIDED report's `the report was made promptly`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Reading B: "promptly" means within a number of days of the event or proposal.  The deadline is the last prompt day, an absolute date.
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
      nDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`F5.1 B: report the matter within a number of days of the event or proposal` interp matter timing nDays MEANS
    PARTY `a registered charity`
    MUST `report a matter to the Commissioner` matter
    WITHIN 0 OF (`Art 13(6) the last prompt day` interp (timing's `date of the event or proposal`) nDays)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a registered charity` BECAUSE "Article 13(6): the matter was not reported within the number of days of the event or proposal"

-- Reading C: "promptly" means within a number of days of the charity becoming aware of the matter.
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
      nDays IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`F5.1 C: report the matter within a number of days of the charity becoming aware of it` interp matter timing nDays MEANS
    PARTY `a registered charity`
    MUST `report a matter to the Commissioner` matter
    WITHIN 0 OF (`Art 13(6) the last prompt day` interp (timing's `date the charity became aware of the matter`) nDays)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a registered charity` BECAUSE "Article 13(6): the matter was not reported within the number of days of the charity becoming aware of it"

@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
      report IS A `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(6) the duty to report on the reading of promptly` interp matter timing report MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `how promptness is measured`
    WHEN `an input judgement that the report was made promptly`
        THEN `F5.1 A: report the matter, promptness being an input judgement` matter report
    WHEN `a number of days from the event or proposal` nDays
        THEN `F5.1 B: report the matter within a number of days of the event or proposal` interp matter timing nDays
    WHEN `a number of days from the charity becoming aware of the matter` nDays
        THEN `F5.1 C: report the matter within a number of days of the charity becoming aware of it` interp matter timing nDays

-- src:383 | (6) A registered charity must promptly report to the Commissioner –
@ref Article 13(6) (src:383)
@export The duty of a registered charity to promptly report to the Commissioner a matter that falls within a paragraph of Article 13(6), as a regulative rule on the reading of "promptly" given (an input judgement, or a number of days from the event or from the charity's awareness); it binds only a registered charity and only a matter within the paragraph
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.1 decides what promptly means
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the requirement of Article 11(4)(c)
      `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity meets the requirement of Article 11(4)(d)
      `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the charity's name is, on what is now known, undesirable under Article 12(1)
      matter IS A `Matter to report under Article 13(6)` @desc The matter and the facts its paragraph turns on
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)` @desc The day of the event or proposal and the day the charity became aware of the matter
      report IS A `Report of a matter under Article 13(6)` @desc The report, if one has been made, and the judgement that it was prompt
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(6) the registered charity must promptly report the matter` interp `the entity is a registered charity` `the registered charity` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` matter timing report MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a registered charity`
       AND `Art 13(6) the matter falls within the paragraph` `the registered charity` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(c) is met` `the requirement of Article 11(4)(d) is met` `the name is undesirable under Article 12(1)` matter
    THEN `Art 13(6) the duty to report on the reading of promptly` interp matter timing report
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:391 | (h) any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(6)(h) (src:391)
@export The Minister's power to prescribe by Order a further matter that a registered charity must promptly report, as a regulative rule; what the Order prescribes is an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(6)(h) the Minister may by Order prescribe a further matter to be reported` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order` `a further matter that a registered charity must promptly report, Article 13(6)(h)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(7) The annual return`

-- Fork F5.2 (period P9).  Article 13(7) speaks of "the year to which the return relates" and does not define "year"; Schedule 1 paragraph 4(8) says
-- "calendar year" when it means one.  Reading A (taken): the calendar year containing the reference day.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`F5.2 A: the calendar year containing` day MEANS
    `Year to which an annual return relates` OF (YMD (DATE_YEAR day) 1 1), (YMD (DATE_YEAR day) 12 31)

-- Reading B: the charity's own financial year containing the reference day.  A financial year ending on 29 February is not modelled (YMD refuses the
-- date in a year with no 29 February).
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN end IS A `Day on which a financial year ends`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`F5.2 B: the financial year ending as given, containing` end day MEANS
    `Year to which an annual return relates` OF firstDay, lastDay
    WHERE
        endThisYear MEANS YMD (DATE_YEAR day) (end's month) (end's day)
        lastDay MEANS IF day AT MOST endThisYear
                      THEN endThisYear
                      ELSE YMD (DATE_YEAR day PLUS 1) (end's month) (end's day)
        firstDay MEANS (YMD (DATE_YEAR lastDay MINUS 1) (end's month) (end's day)) PLUS 1

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN yearEnd IS A MAYBE `Day on which a financial year ends`
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`F5.2 B: the financial year containing` yearEnd day MEANS
    CONSIDER yearEnd
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `the financial year end of the charity is not given`
    WHEN JUST end THEN `F5.2 B: the financial year ending as given, containing` end day

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`the financial year end of the charity is not given` MEANS
    REFUSE "the financial year end of the charity is not given, so the financial year cannot be found"

-- F5.11: the anniversary of a registration, k years on.  Reading A (taken): a registration made on 29 February has its anniversary on the last day of
-- February in a year with no 29 February (daydate `add years` clamps).  Reading B: the day rolls forward to 1 March.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN registered IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F5.11 A: the anniversary clamped to the last day of the month` registered years MEANS
    `add years` registered years

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN registered IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`F5.11 B: the anniversary rolled forward` registered years MEANS
    Date (DATE_DAY registered) (DATE_MONTH registered) (DATE_YEAR registered PLUS years)

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      registered IS A DATE
      years IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 13(7) the anniversary of the registration` interp registered years MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the anniversary of a registration made on 29 February`
    WHEN `the last day of February (the day is clamped, as daydate add years does)`
        THEN `F5.11 A: the anniversary clamped to the last day of the month` registered years
    WHEN `the first day of March (the day rolls forward)`
        THEN `F5.11 B: the anniversary rolled forward` registered years

-- Reading C: the twelve months from each anniversary of registration, the anniversary day being the first day and the day before the next anniversary
-- the last.  A day before the registration is in no year of the charity's return.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      registered IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`F5.2 C: the number of whole years from the registration to the start of the year containing` interp registered day MEANS
    IF `Art 13(7) the anniversary of the registration` interp registered lastTry AT MOST day
    THEN lastTry
    ELSE lastTry MINUS 1
    WHERE
        lastTry MEANS DATE_YEAR day MINUS DATE_YEAR registered

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      registered IS A DATE
      day IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`F5.2 C: the year from the anniversary of registration containing` interp registered day MEANS
    IF day LESS THAN registered
    THEN `the reference day is before the charity was registered`
    ELSE `Year to which an annual return relates` OF firstDay, lastDay
    WHERE
        yearsDone MEANS `F5.2 C: the number of whole years from the registration to the start of the year containing` interp registered day
        firstDay MEANS `Art 13(7) the anniversary of the registration` interp registered yearsDone
        lastDay MEANS (`Art 13(7) the anniversary of the registration` interp registered (yearsDone PLUS 1)) MINUS 1

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`the reference day is before the charity was registered` MEANS
    REFUSE "the reference day is before the charity was registered, so it is in no year of the charity's return"

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
@export The year to which an annual return relates, for a reference day inside it: the calendar year, the charity's financial year, or the twelve months from each anniversary of registration, as the reading of "year" in the interpretation says
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.2 decides what year means (and F5.11 how a 29 February registration is counted)
      `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity` @desc What the register holds about the charity, including the date it was registered
      `the financial year end` IS A MAYBE `Day on which a financial year ends` @desc The month and day on which the charity's financial year ends; NOTHING if not known (needed only for the financial-year reading)
      `a day in the year` IS A DATE @desc Any day inside the year to which the return relates
GIVETH A `Year to which an annual return relates`
`Art 13(7) the year to which the return relates` interp `the registered charity` `the financial year end` `a day in the year` MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the meaning of the year of an annual return`
    WHEN `the calendar year`
        THEN `F5.2 A: the calendar year containing` `a day in the year`
    WHEN `the charity's own financial year`
        THEN `F5.2 B: the financial year containing` `the financial year end` `a day in the year`
    WHEN `the twelve months from each anniversary of registration`
        THEN `F5.2 C: the year from the anniversary of registration containing` interp (`the registered charity`'s `date registered`) `a day in the year`

-- Fork F5.13.  A matter "arising during the year": Reading A (taken): the date of the event or proposal.  Reading B: the day the charity became aware.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
GIVETH A DATE
`Art 13(7) the date on which the matter arises` interp timing MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the date on which a matter arises`
    WHEN `the date of the event or proposal` THEN timing's `date of the event or proposal`
    WHEN `the date the charity became aware of the matter` THEN timing's `date the charity became aware of the matter`

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates`
      timing IS A `Timing of a matter under Article 13(6)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` interp year timing MEANS
        `Art 13(7) the date on which the matter arises` interp timing AT LEAST year's `first day`
    AND `Art 13(7) the date on which the matter arises` interp timing AT MOST year's `last day`

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates`
      m IS A `Matter arising for the annual return`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(7) the return covers the matter if it must` interp year m MEANS
    NOT (    m's `falls within paragraph (6)`
         AND `Art 13(7) the matter arose during the year to which the return relates` interp year (m's timing))
    OR m's `the annual return gives information about it`

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
@export Whether an annual return contains what Article 13(7) requires: information about every matter within Article 13(6) that arose during the year to which the return relates, and about every other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for the purpose
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.13 decides when a matter arises
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates` @desc The year to which the return relates
      matters IS A LIST OF `Matter arising for the annual return` @desc Every matter the charity had in or near the year, with whether it falls within Article 13(6) and whether the return gives information about it
      `the return gives information about every matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the return contains information about every other matter that an Order under Article 13(7) prescribes for the return
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(7) the annual return contains the information paragraph (7) requires` interp year matters `the return gives information about every matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(7)` MEANS
        all (GIVEN m YIELD `Art 13(7) the return covers the matter if it must` interp year m) matters
    AND `the return gives information about every matter prescribed by Order under Article 13(7)`

-- The duty to send, with the time the Law leaves to an Order (13(8)).  With no due date the Law states no time and the rule carries no WITHIN.
-- Fork F5.5: Reading A (taken), a return sent on the due date is timely (WITHIN 0 OF the due date is inclusive).  Reading B: it must be sent before.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392), 13(8) (src:393)
GIVEN dueDate IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`F5.5 A: send the annual return on or before the due date` dueDate MEANS
    PARTY `a registered charity`
    MUST `send the annual return to the Commissioner`
    WITHIN 0 OF dueDate
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a registered charity` BECAUSE "Article 13(7): the annual return was not sent by the due date set by the Order"

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392), 13(8) (src:393)
GIVEN dueDate IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`F5.5 B: send the annual return before the due date` dueDate MEANS
    PARTY `a registered charity`
    MUST `send the annual return to the Commissioner`
    WITHIN 0 OF (dueDate MINUS 1)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `a registered charity` BECAUSE "Article 13(7): the annual return was not sent before the due date set by the Order"

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392), 13(8) (src:393)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      dueDate IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(7) the duty to send by the due date on the reading of timely` interp dueDate MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `whether a return sent on the due date is timely`
    WHEN `timely if sent on or before the due date` THEN `F5.5 A: send the annual return on or before the due date` dueDate
    WHEN `late unless sent before the due date` THEN `F5.5 B: send the annual return before the due date` dueDate

@ref Article 13(7) (src:392), 13(8) (src:393)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(7) the duty to send with the time an Order sets` interp order MEANS
    CONSIDER order's `due date of the annual return`
    WHEN NOTHING
        THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
             MUST `send the annual return to the Commissioner`
             HENCE FULFILLED
    WHEN JUST dueDate THEN `Art 13(7) the duty to send by the due date on the reading of timely` interp dueDate

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
@export The duty of a registered charity to send an annual return to the Commissioner, as a regulative rule: with the time (and so the breach) that an Order under Article 13(7) and (8) sets, and with no time where no Order sets one
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.5 decides whether a return sent on the due date is timely
      `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` @desc What the Order under Article 13(7) and (8) provides; both its due date and its consequence are NOTHING if no Order is encoded
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(7) the registered charity must send an annual return` interp `the entity is a registered charity` order MEANS
    IF `the entity is a registered charity`
    THEN `Art 13(7) the duty to send with the time an Order sets` interp order
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(8) The format and timing of the annual return, and the consequences of lateness`

-- The Law fixes no due date and names no consequence of lateness: both are for the Order, and none is among the sources.  A question that needs
-- them is a named refusal, not FALSE and not a default.
@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`no Order under Article 13(8) fixing the due date of the annual return is encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no Order under Article 13(8) fixing the due date of the annual return is encoded in this model"

@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
GIVETH A STRING
`no Order under Article 13(8) stating the consequences of lateness is encoded in this model` MEANS
    REFUSE "no Order under Article 13(8) stating the consequences of lateness is encoded in this model"

-- src:393 | (8) An Order under paragraph (7) may also make provision as to the format and timing of the annual return, the consequences of lateness, and the content of any entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return.
@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
@export Whether an annual return sent on a day is late, by the due date an Order under Article 13(7) and (8) sets: whether a return sent on the due date itself is late is a fork; with no due date the answer is a refusal
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.5 decides whether a return sent on the due date is timely
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` @desc What the Order provides; the due date is NOTHING if no Order is encoded
      `the day the return was sent` IS A DATE @desc The day the annual return was sent to the Commissioner
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(8) the annual return is late` interp order `the day the return was sent` MEANS
    CONSIDER order's `due date of the annual return`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no Order under Article 13(8) fixing the due date of the annual return is encoded in this model`
    WHEN JUST dueDate THEN
        CONSIDER interp's `whether a return sent on the due date is timely`
        WHEN `timely if sent on or before the due date` THEN `the day the return was sent` GREATER THAN dueDate
        WHEN `late unless sent before the due date` THEN `the day the return was sent` AT LEAST dueDate

-- src:393 | (8) An Order under paragraph (7) may also make provision as to the format and timing of the annual return, the consequences of lateness, and the content of any entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return.
@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
@export The consequence of a late annual return that an Order under Article 13(7) and (8) states; a refusal if no Order states one
GIVEN order IS AN `Order under Article 13(7) and (8)` @desc What the Order provides; its consequence of lateness is NOTHING if no Order is encoded
GIVETH A STRING
`Art 13(8) the consequence of lateness` order MEANS
    CONSIDER order's `consequence of lateness`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN `no Order under Article 13(8) stating the consequences of lateness is encoded in this model`
    WHEN JUST consequence THEN consequence

-- The Minister's powers over the annual return.  (7): "any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order".  (8): an Order under (7) may also provide
-- for format and timing, the consequences of lateness and the register entries; paragraph (8) confers no Order of its own, so those provisions are
-- made in an Order under (7).
@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of an Order under Article 13`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(8) paragraph (8) lets an Order under paragraph (7) cover the subject` subject MEANS
    CONSIDER subject
    WHEN `the format and timing of the annual return, Article 13(8)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the consequences of lateness of the annual return, Article 13(8)` THEN TRUE
    WHEN `the entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return, Article 13(8)` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:392 | (7) A registered charity must send an annual return to the Commissioner, containing information as to any matter falling within paragraph (6) arising during the year to which the return relates, and as to any other matter prescribed by the Minister by Order for this purpose.
@ref Article 13(7) (src:392)
@export The Minister's power to prescribe by Order a further matter that an annual return must contain, as a regulative rule; what the Order prescribes is an input
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(7) the Minister may by Order prescribe a further matter for the annual return` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order` `a further matter that an annual return must contain, Article 13(7)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:393 | (8) An Order under paragraph (7) may also make provision as to the format and timing of the annual return, the consequences of lateness, and the content of any entries to be made on the register in respect of the annual return.
@ref Article 13(8) (src:393)
@export The Minister's power, in an Order under Article 13(7), to provide for the format and timing of the annual return, the consequences of lateness and the register entries made in respect of the annual return, as a regulative rule; it covers only those subjects, and only in an Order under paragraph (7)
GIVEN subject IS A `Subject of an Order under Article 13` @desc The subject the provision is about
      `the provision is made in an Order under paragraph (7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the provision is made in an Order under Article 13(7), which is the only Order paragraph (8) speaks of
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(8) the Minister may by Order provide for the format and timing of the annual return` subject `the provision is made in an Order under paragraph (7)` MEANS
    IF     `the provision is made in an Order under paragraph (7)`
       AND `Art 13(8) paragraph (8) lets an Order under paragraph (7) cover the subject` subject
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `make an Order` subject
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(9) Payments to a governor: the Minister's Order`

-- src:394 | (9) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:395 | (a) require a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of any payment made, during the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the registered charity to a governor, or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor;
@ref Article 13(9)(a) (src:394-395)
@export The Minister's power to require by Order a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of payment made in the year to a governor or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor, as a regulative rule
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(9)(a) the Minister may by Order require payment details in the annual return` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order` `the details of payments to a governor that an annual return must include, Article 13(9)(a)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:394 | (9) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:396 | (b) require a registered charity to provide to the Commissioner a statement of its current intentions as to making any payments of such a prescribed description in future;
@ref Article 13(9)(b) (src:394) (src:396)
@export The Minister's power to require by Order a registered charity to provide to the Commissioner a statement of its current intentions as to making payments of the prescribed description in future, as a regulative rule
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(9)(b) the Minister may by Order require a statement of intentions` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order` `the statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor, Article 13(9)(b)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- src:394 | (9) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:397 | (c) provide for the entry on the register by the Commissioner of the details included under sub-paragraph (a) in the charity’s latest annual return, and of the statement provided under sub-paragraph (b).
@ref Article 13(9)(c) (src:394) (src:397)
@export The Minister's power to provide by Order for the Commissioner to enter on the register the payment details in the charity's latest annual return and the statement of intentions, as a regulative rule
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(9)(c) the Minister may by Order provide for entry on the register` MEANS
    PARTY `the Minister`
    MAY `make an Order` `the entry on the register of those details and of that statement, Article 13(9)(c)`
    HENCE FULFILLED

-- Integration point IP29.  An Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity if there is such an Order that requires at least one of the
-- three things and no valid Order under Article 13(10) disapplies it for a charity of the prescribed description.  An Order that applies subject to a
-- modification still applies.  The Order under 13(9) is MAYBE: NOTHING means no Order is encoded.
@ref Article 13(9) (src:394)
GIVEN order IS AN `Order under Article 13(9)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9) the Order requires or provides something` order MEANS
        order's `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)`
    OR  order's `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)`
    OR  order's `provides for entry on the register, Article 13(9)(c)`

-- src:395 | (a) require a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of any payment made, during the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the registered charity to a governor, or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor;
@ref Article 13(9)(a) (src:395) -- the details the Order requires
GIVEN payment IS A `Payment to a governor or a connected person`
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` payment year MEANS
        payment's `date of the payment` AT LEAST year's `first day`
    AND payment's `date of the payment` AT MOST year's `last day`

-- src:395 | (a) require a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of any payment made, during the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the registered charity to a governor, or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor;
@ref Article 13(9)(a) (src:395)
@export Whether a payment is one whose details an Order under Article 13(9)(a) requires the registered charity to include in its annual return: made in the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the charity, to a governor or a person having a prescribed connection with a governor, and of the prescribed description
GIVEN `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity (not relieved by an Order under Article 13(10))
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc What the Order requires
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates` @desc The year to which the return relates (fork F5.2 decides what the year is)
      payment IS A `Payment to a governor or a connected person` @desc The payment and the facts the Order's description turns on
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order year payment MEANS
        `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
    AND order's `requires details of prescribed payments in the annual return, Article 13(9)(a)`
    AND payment's `made by or on behalf of the registered charity`
    AND (   payment's `made to a governor of the charity`
         OR payment's `made to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor`)
    AND payment's `of a description prescribed by the Order`
    AND `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls within the year to which the return relates` payment year

-- The annual return of a charity to which an Order under 13(9)(a) applies must give the details of every payment that falls to be included.
-- src:395 | (a) require a registered charity to include in its annual return details of a prescribed description of any payment made, during the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the registered charity to a governor, or to a person having a prescribed connection with a governor;
@ref Article 13(9)(a) (src:395)
@export Whether an annual return gives the details of every payment that an Order under Article 13(9)(a) requires it to include (a payment made in the year to which the return relates, by or on behalf of the charity, to a governor or a person connected with a governor, of the prescribed description)
GIVEN `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc What the Order requires
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates` @desc The year to which the return relates
      payments IS A LIST OF `Payment to a governor or a connected person` @desc Every payment the charity made in or near the year, with whether the annual return gives its details
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9)(a) the annual return gives the details of the payments the Order requires` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order year payments MEANS
    all (GIVEN payment YIELD `Art 13(9)(a) the return covers the payment if it must` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order year payment) payments

@ref Article 13(9)(a) (src:395)
GIVEN `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(9)`
      year IS A `Year to which an annual return relates`
      payment IS A `Payment to a governor or a connected person`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9)(a) the return covers the payment if it must` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order year payment MEANS
    NOT `Art 13(9)(a) the payment falls to be included in the annual return` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order year payment
    OR payment's `the annual return gives its details`

-- (b): once an Order under 13(9)(b) applies, the registered charity must provide the statement.  The Law fixes no time (the Order may), and none is in
-- the sources, so the rule carries no WITHIN.
-- src:396 | (b) require a registered charity to provide to the Commissioner a statement of its current intentions as to making any payments of such a prescribed description in future;
@ref Article 13(9)(b) (src:396)
@export The duty of a registered charity, once an Order under Article 13(9)(b) applies to it, to provide the Commissioner with a statement of its current intentions as to making payments of the prescribed description in future, as a regulative rule; the Law states no time and the Order's is not among the sources
GIVEN `the entity is a registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the entity is entered for the time being in the general or the restricted section of the register
      `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the charity
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc What the Order requires
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(9)(b) the registered charity must provide a statement of its current intentions` `the entity is a registered charity` `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` order MEANS
    IF     `the entity is a registered charity`
       AND `an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity`
       AND order's `requires a statement of current intentions as to such payments, Article 13(9)(b)`
    THEN PARTY `a registered charity`
         MUST `provide the Commissioner with a statement of current intentions as to payments to a governor`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§§ `13(10) The Minister's Order relieving small charities`

-- The power is the Minister's, to be used "after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested
-- registered charities", for a description of charity that "appears to the Minister to require relief" (a) or for a modification that "appears to the
-- Minister to give reasonable relief" (b).  The consultation is a fact; the Minister's opinion is an input.
@ref Article 13(10) (src:398-400)
GIVEN order IS AN `Order under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` order MEANS
        "after consulting the Commissioner" ... order's `the Minister consulted the Commissioner`
    AND "and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities"
        ... order's `the Minister consulted a body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities`
    AND "(a)/(b): relief by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise"
        ... order's `it appears to the Minister that the description of charity requires relief from the burden of the provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise, of charities of that description`

-- src:398 | (10) The Minister may by Order, after consulting the Commissioner and any body appearing to the Minister to be representative of interested registered charities, provide that any provision of paragraph (6) or (7), or of any Order under paragraph (7), (8) or (9) –
-- src:399 | (a) does not apply to a prescribed description of charity appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description; or
-- src:400 | (b) applies to a prescribed description of charity only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description.
@ref Article 13(10) (src:398-400)
@export The Minister's power to relieve a prescribed description of small charity by Order from a provision of Article 13(6) or (7) or of an Order under Article 13(7), (8) or (9), as a regulative rule: it is open only after the two consultations and on the Minister's opinion that the description needs relief
GIVEN order IS AN `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The proposed relief Order and the facts of the consultation and of the Minister's opinion
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order relieve small charities` order MEANS
    IF `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` order
    THEN PARTY `the Minister`
         MAY `make an Order` `relief for a prescribed description of charity, Article 13(10)`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- Fork F5.3 (trap T18).  Does the provision named in the relief Order reach the provision in question?  Paragraph (8) confers no Order of its own: an
-- Order under (7) may contain provision made by virtue of (8).
-- Reading A (taken): "an Order under paragraph (8)" means the Order under (7) as extended by (8), so an Order naming it reaches the provisions of an
-- Order under (7) that are made by virtue of (8).  Reading B (literal): there is no Order under (8), so an Order naming one reaches nothing.
@ref Article 13(10) (src:398-400)
GIVEN named IS A `Provision that an Order under Article 13(10) may relieve`
      target IS A `Provision in question under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.3 A: the Order under paragraph (8) is the Order under paragraph (7) as extended` named target MEANS
    CONSIDER named
    WHEN `a provision of paragraph (6)` THEN target EQUALS `a provision of paragraph (6)`
    WHEN `a provision of paragraph (7)` THEN target EQUALS `a provision of paragraph (7)`
    WHEN `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7)`
        THEN (   target EQUALS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) not made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
              OR target EQUALS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`)
    WHEN `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)`
        THEN target EQUALS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (7) made by virtue of paragraph (8)`
    WHEN `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)` THEN target EQUALS `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`

@ref Article 13(10) (src:398-400)
GIVEN named IS A `Provision that an Order under Article 13(10) may relieve`
      target IS A `Provision in question under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`F5.3 B: no Order exists under paragraph (8)` named target MEANS
    CONSIDER named
    WHEN `a provision of an Order under paragraph (8)` THEN FALSE
    OTHERWISE `F5.3 A: the Order under paragraph (8) is the Order under paragraph (7) as extended` named target

@ref Article 13(10) (src:398-400)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      named IS A `Provision that an Order under Article 13(10) may relieve`
      target IS A `Provision in question under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(10) the relief Order names the provision` interp named target MEANS
    CONSIDER interp's `the meaning of an Order under paragraph (8)`
    WHEN `the Order under paragraph (7) as extended by paragraph (8)`
        THEN `F5.3 A: the Order under paragraph (8) is the Order under paragraph (7) as extended` named target
    WHEN `no Order exists under paragraph (8)`
        THEN `F5.3 B: no Order exists under paragraph (8)` named target

-- src:399 | (a) does not apply to a prescribed description of charity appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description; or
-- src:400 | (b) applies to a prescribed description of charity only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description.
@ref Article 13(10)(a) and (b) (src:399-400)
@export What an Order under Article 13(10) does, for a charity of the description it prescribes, to a provision of Article 13(6) or (7) or of an Order under Article 13(7), (8) or (9): none (the provision applies in full), disapplication (a), or application only subject to a prescribed modification (b); an Order made without the consultations has no effect
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points; fork F5.3 decides what an Order under paragraph (8) is
      order IS AN `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The relief Order, the facts of its making, and whether the charity is of the description it prescribes
      target IS A `Provision in question under Article 13(10)` @desc The provision whose application to the charity is in question
GIVETH AN `Effect of an Order under Article 13(10) on a provision`
`Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` interp order target MEANS
    IF     `Art 13(10) the Minister may by Order provide the relief` order
       AND order's `the charity is of the prescribed description`
       AND `Art 13(10) the relief Order names the provision` interp (order's provision) target
    THEN CONSIDER order's relief
         WHEN `relief by disapplication, Article 13(10)(a)` THEN `the provision does not apply to the charity`
         WHEN `relief by modification, Article 13(10)(b)` modification
             THEN `the provision applies to the charity only subject to a modification` modification
    ELSE `the provision applies in full`

-- IP29.  A relief Order that disapplies "a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)" for a charity of the description takes the charity out of the
-- Order under 13(9) altogether, whichever of its three requirements; a modification leaves the Order applying.
@ref Article 13(10)(a) (src:399)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      relief IS AN `Order under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(10) the relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9)` interp relief MEANS
    CONSIDER `Art 13(10) the effect of the relief Order on the provision` interp relief `a provision of an Order under paragraph (9)`
    WHEN `the provision does not apply to the charity` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

@ref Article 13(10)(a) (src:399)
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14`
      reliefs IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(10) a relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9) for the charity` interp reliefs MEANS
    any (GIVEN relief YIELD `Art 13(10) the relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9)` interp relief) reliefs

-- src:394 | (9) The Minister may by Order –
-- src:399 | (a) does not apply to a prescribed description of charity appearing to the Minister to require relief from the burden of that provision by virtue of the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description; or
-- src:400 | (b) applies to a prescribed description of charity only subject to a modification prescribed by the Order, being a modification that appears to the Minister to give reasonable relief from the burden of that provision, having regard to the small size, or lack of resources or expertise of charities of that description.
@ref Article 13(9) (src:394) and 13(10) (src:399-400)
@export Whether an Order under Article 13(9) (payment details, statement of intentions, entry on the register) applies to the registered charity: there is such an Order, and no valid Order under Article 13(10) disapplies it for a charity of the description it prescribes
GIVEN interp IS AN `Interpretation of Articles 13 and 14` @desc The readings of the Law's open points
      order IS A MAYBE `Order under Article 13(9)` @desc The Order under Article 13(9); NOTHING if no Order is encoded
      reliefs IS A LIST OF `Order under Article 13(10)` @desc The Orders under Article 13(10) made; empty if none
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(9) an Order under Article 13(9) applies to the registered charity` interp order reliefs MEANS
    CONSIDER order
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST theOrder THEN
            `Art 13(9) the Order requires or provides something` theOrder
        AND NOT `Art 13(10) a relief Order disapplies an Order under paragraph (9) for the charity` interp reliefs

§§§ `13(12) Regulations under Article 11(7)`

-- "If the States make Regulations under Article 11(7), those Regulations may also make provision requiring a registered charity or its governors (or
-- both) to avoid, or report and remedy, a situation arising at a time after registration, ...".  The power is the States'; what the Regulations require
-- is an input.  The situation is one for which "if the charity were at that time applying for registration, there would be grounds under those
-- Regulations to refuse that application": a fact about the Regulations, supplied.
-- src:404 | (12) If the States make Regulations under Article 11(7), those Regulations may also make provision requiring a registered charity or its governors (or both) to avoid, or report and remedy, a situation arising at a time after registration, being a situation in which, if the charity were at that time applying for registration, there would be grounds under those Regulations to refuse that application.
@ref Article 13(12) (src:404)
@export The States' power, in Regulations under Article 11(7), to require a registered charity or its governors (or both) to avoid, or report and remedy, a situation arising after registration in which there would be grounds under those Regulations to refuse an application, as a regulative rule: it is open only if the States make Regulations under Article 11(7)
GIVEN `the States make Regulations under Article 11(7)` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the States are making Regulations under Article 11(7) (further grounds on which an application must or may be refused)
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Legal actor` `Act under Article 13`
`Art 13(12) the States may require a charity to avoid or report and remedy a later ground for refusal` `the States make Regulations under Article 11(7)` MEANS
    IF `the States make Regulations under Article 11(7)`
    THEN PARTY `the States`
         MAY `make Regulations requiring a charity or its governors to avoid, or report and remedy, a later ground for refusal`
         HENCE FULFILLED
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- src:404 | (12) If the States make Regulations under Article 11(7), those Regulations may also make provision requiring a registered charity or its governors (or both) to avoid, or report and remedy, a situation arising at a time after registration, being a situation in which, if the charity were at that time applying for registration, there would be grounds under those Regulations to refuse that application.
@ref Article 13(12) (src:404)
@export Whether a situation is one that Regulations under Article 11(7) may require a registered charity or its governors to avoid, or report and remedy: it arose at a time after registration, and an application made at that time would have grounds under the Regulations for refusal
GIVEN `the situation arose at a time after registration` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the situation arose after the charity was registered
      `there would be grounds under the Regulations to refuse an application made at that time` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, if the charity were applying for registration at that time, there would be grounds under the Regulations under Article 11(7) to refuse the application
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`Art 13(12) the situation is one the Regulations may require the charity or its governors to avoid or to report and remedy` `the situation arose at a time after registration` `there would be grounds under the Regulations to refuse an application made at that time` MEANS
        "a situation arising at a time after registration"
    ... `the situation arose at a time after registration`
    AND "being a situation in which, if the charity were at that time applying for registration, there would be grounds under those Regulations to refuse that application"
    ... `there would be grounds under the Regulations to refuse an application made at that time`
